  "CORRECTED": {
    "the exceptional-locus coordinates": "WAS listed NOT PROVED, computed but not checked. Now proved -- all seven, 21 tangencies. sqrt(6) is handled as sqrt(2)*sqrt(3) rather than as a third atom, so the four sqrt(6) solutions share one residual across all twelve of their tangencies.",
    "the eight flagship coordinates": "WAS listed NOT PROVED: computed in exact arithmetic but not checked in Lean. Now proved. All eight circles of d=4, rho=1 are stated in closed form and discharged against the geometric tangency predicates -- 24 tangencies, zero residual, sorryAx absent. The obstacle was never the geometry: it was Lean.Meta.acLt blowing up on nested (1+1) constant trees under distribution. Compressing the constant into the variable (v = 3h with 2v^2 = 9, kappa = sqrt21/3 with 3kappa^2 = 7) keeps every constant out of the distribution and all twelve identities close at once.",
    "list-cardinality form": "WAS listed NOT PROVED, on the grounds that MachLib is Mathlib-free and has no Finset layer. The premise was true and the inference was wrong: List, List.length and List.Nodup are Lean CORE, not Mathlib, and Finset is not needed for a finite enumeration. Now proved. eight_solutions delivers a List of length 8, Nodup, every entry a positive-radius solution of its mode. The mode half is stronger still: allModes_length and allModes_nodup depend on NO AXIOMS AT ALL, and allModes_complete on propext alone."
  },
